    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this case is decided on the trip's own records, and both sides end up asking for the same number.\n\nTHE DEVIATION IS ESTABLISHED. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00302) measures the trip at 28.2 km against the booked optimal of 22.0 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-00302). The excess is 6.2 km, which is 28.18% of optimal. Both tests in POL-RD-01 pass — above 20% and above 0.8 km — so a route deviation is established. The trace is genuinely usable: 235 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds, so it is NOT impaired under POL-RD-07 and the 6.2 km figure cannot be written off as a data artefact.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S TRAFFIC EXPLANATION FAILS. The driver says 'SLE was heavy at the CTE merge so I stayed on CTE all the way down.' That is an external-traffic assertion, and POL-RD-08 requires the driver to point to a specific artifact. He points to none. The only traffic advisory for this trip, EV-ADVIS-00302-01, is MISSING — admissibility status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT (BLOCKING). No advisory covers the SLE or the CTE in this window, so the comparison POL-RD-03 requires cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and under POL-RD-13 the assertion carries no weight. The driver did not cite the missing advisory in support of his excuse, so this is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation: the deviation simply stands at the measured 6.2 km against the booked 22.0 km.\n\nNO OTHER EXCULATORY ROUTE APPLIES. There is no rider-requested detour: the chat log (EV-CHAT-00302) is a complete export with zero messages and the trip record shows chat_message_count 0, so POL-RD-04 cannot be met and POL-RD-14 has nothing to consider. The destination was not moved — pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at, original_pickup and original_dropoff are all null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 does not re-quote the route. The vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. The rider's description of 'all the way round via the CTE' overstates the record: the first gantry, BKE (Woodlands towards PIE) at 1.50, is flagged on_optimal_route true with a 0.0 m nearest fix, so the driver began on the optimal corridor and the deviation is confined to the tail. That does not change the outcome, because the excess still clears the establishment gate.\n\nTHE REFUND IS ARITHMETIC. The fare is METERED on EV-FARE-00302 and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-11 does not displace POL-RD-02. The surge multiplier is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier on EV-FARE-00302 and is 1.2; it multiplies both the charged fare and the recomputed optimal fare, so it explains none of the gap. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 22.0 km + 0.28 x 28.0 min) x 1.2) + 0.80 platform fee + 1.50 on-optimal-route ERP = (28.14 x 1.2) + 2.30 = 33.768 + 2.30 = 36.068. Charged total is 48.34. Refund = 48.34 - 36.068 = 12.272, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05, giving 12.30. That is above the 0.50 de minimis and only 25.4% of charged_total, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND, not the FULL_REFUND that would need 90%.\n\nERP. The rider's request for the extra ERP back is already answered inside the 12.30. Three gantries were charged totalling 4.50: BKE (Woodlands towards PIE) 1.50, on the optimal route; CTE (Braddell Rd towards City) 2.00 and CTE (Moulmein Rd towards City) 1.00, both off it. Under POL-RD-09(1) the off-route ERP of 3.00 is comprehended in the recomputation, because the recomputed fare counts only the 1.50 on-route gantry; adding 3.00 on top of 12.30 would be the double-count the clause forbids. These lines are itemised for transparency only. Both off-route crossings were real — nearest fixes 0.0 m from each gantry — so there is no phantom line under POL-RD-09(4), the airport surcharge is 0.00 on a trip that does not touch an airport, and no billing-integrity referral fires.\n\nDRIVER PROFILE. No adverse finding attaches. deviation_flags_90d is 1 and completed_trips_90d is 70 — a ratio of 0.014, far under the 0.05 the POL-RD-06 test needs and under the 3-flag alternative — so no repeat-deviation pattern is established. The excess is also below the materiality line (under 50% and under 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 FULL_REFUND uplift and the driver-conduct referral are not triggered either way. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is a context-only field under POL-GEN-01 and was not used for any finding. The rider profile likewise raises no obstacle: deviation_claims_60d is 0, so POL-RD-08's extra corroboration requirement is not engaged.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND EXECUTION. Every artifact that carries a deciding fact — EV-GPS-00302, EV-TRIP-00302 and EV-FARE-00302 — is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0 and my confidence is 0.9. One claim from the rider's side was discarded at the mechanical stage: an assertion that no POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires, discarded because it cited the MISSING advisory without disclosing its issue code, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires (see the discarded-claims record). Nothing turns on it, because the monetary road here runs through POL-RD-13 and the same conclusion is reached by the clauses that remain. The monetary effect of 12.30 exceeds the execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so under POL-GEN-05 this ruling issues but is held for release by a human reviewer rather than executed automatically. Either party may also appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
